WEBVTT

00:00:14.370 --> 00:00:16.370
Please cut your hair.

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:20.950
I realize the affront of what I ask.

00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:23.950
But since we cannot change
your face or your voice,

00:00:23.950 --> 00:00:27.370
there is no other way to fool everyone else.

00:00:34.450 --> 00:00:36.160
I will step out.

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:42.120
We will have to think of
a new name for you, as well.

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:48.490
Henceforth, you will have to live
under an assumed identity, after all.

00:01:03.910 --> 00:01:06.830
This has definitely been hard on her.

00:01:06.830 --> 00:01:09.370
She just watched her father get killed,

00:01:09.370 --> 00:01:13.040
and now she is being driven from her land.

00:01:13.040 --> 00:01:18.910
The princess is still too young
to accept such a harsh reality.

00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:56.870
The fantastical paradise, Magonia.

00:02:56.870 --> 00:03:02.790
It is brimming with a "great power"
that can make any wish come true.

00:03:02.790 --> 00:03:08.620
Islands floating in the sky; tales of giants
and princesses; crimson dragons--

00:03:08.620 --> 00:03:12.740
many legends and fables from Magonian lore

00:03:12.740 --> 00:03:17.540
are age-old tales,
familiar to all the kingdom's people.

00:03:17.540 --> 00:03:21.200
But then, these imaginary creatures
suddenly began appearing

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:23.950
throughout the kingdom of Hortensia.

00:03:23.950 --> 00:03:28.040
As days turned into months,
the people had to accept

00:03:28.040 --> 00:03:30.990
that the existence of these monsters was real.

00:03:30.990 --> 00:03:33.950
May, 771, New Holy Era

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:50.330
Whew. That should do it.

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:53.370
Never mind that there aren't
that many monsters in Albert,

00:03:53.370 --> 00:03:56.580
I'm surprised that its lord is out here
today putting them down personally.

00:03:56.580 --> 00:04:00.450
Safeguarding the livelihood of
the dominion's people is the lord's duty.

00:04:00.450 --> 00:04:04.040
Usually, it's a job for the knights
or mercenaries, isn't it?

00:04:04.040 --> 00:04:06.950
The time will come when
we have to fight Camellia again.

00:04:06.950 --> 00:04:09.700
I don't want to lay too much
on them before then.

00:04:09.700 --> 00:04:13.700
Besides, I have to get stronger,

00:04:13.700 --> 00:04:15.870
if I'm going to overcome Roy of Camellia.

00:04:19.990 --> 00:04:22.790
Come to think of it, where is Marius today?

00:04:22.790 --> 00:04:26.330
He always joins you when you
go out on monster patrol.

00:04:26.330 --> 00:04:28.620
He's improved his skills plenty as it is.

00:04:28.620 --> 00:04:30.830
I entrusted him with an important mission today.

00:04:33.290 --> 00:04:36.830
It's so heavy <i>moru</i> .
I can't carry it anymore <i>moru</i> .

00:04:36.830 --> 00:04:40.700
I'm so glad you two are lending
me a hand, Marius.

00:04:40.700 --> 00:04:43.490
I'll get you for this, Alfred.

00:04:43.490 --> 00:04:44.950
<i>Moru</i> .

00:04:44.950 --> 00:04:47.990
Oh, are you starting to get tired?
We can switch off.

00:04:47.990 --> 00:04:50.950
No, this is a job for a man, so...

00:04:50.950 --> 00:04:54.700
Huh? What's with the flowers <i>moru</i> ?

00:04:54.700 --> 00:04:59.290
Oh, there's a place I'd like
to visit along the way.

00:05:05.410 --> 00:05:07.870
Whenever I go out on an errand,

00:05:07.870 --> 00:05:11.660
I always come and offer a prayer to Fernando,

00:05:11.660 --> 00:05:15.830
his wife Hortense,
as well as their daughter, Ber.

00:05:15.830 --> 00:05:20.160
Ber-- Alfred's younger sister, Bernadette.

00:05:20.160 --> 00:05:23.240
Qoo would have liked to meet her.

00:05:23.240 --> 00:05:26.450
It must be four years now.

00:05:26.450 --> 00:05:31.790
When all of my relatives passed on,
Fernando took me on as a maid,

00:05:31.790 --> 00:05:37.990
and both Fernando and Ber welcomed me in warmly.

00:05:37.990 --> 00:05:43.490
Ber and I were the same age,
and we got along very well from the start.

00:05:43.490 --> 00:05:47.830
But Ber was born with a weak constitution,

00:05:47.830 --> 00:05:51.370
and she spent every day in her room.

00:05:51.370 --> 00:05:56.990
She was nice, and extremely bright,
and would often read books to me.

00:05:56.990 --> 00:06:01.950
I always enjoyed when she did that. But...

00:06:01.950 --> 00:06:06.160
Ber said goodbye to us without any warning.

00:06:06.160 --> 00:06:11.660
The carriage she was riding in
got caught in a landslide.

00:06:11.660 --> 00:06:18.740
Ber... and all of the other Alberts
are like dear family to me.

00:06:18.740 --> 00:06:24.160
Which is why I work as hard as I can
to keep Alfred from being lonely,

00:06:24.160 --> 00:06:27.120
by doing the cleaning, the laundry, the cooking,

00:06:27.120 --> 00:06:30.370
and bringing life to the manor! Yeah!

00:06:31.620 --> 00:06:34.580
I wish I could do as much as you, Nonnoria.

00:06:34.580 --> 00:06:39.080
No, no! Marius, you still have
a lot on your shoulders!

00:06:39.080 --> 00:06:42.040
Ah, hold on! I said I would carry that!

00:06:47.410 --> 00:06:49.240
Marius! Nonnoria!

00:06:49.240 --> 00:06:51.240
Conny! Doris!

00:06:51.240 --> 00:06:55.540
You two are looking fine today!

00:06:55.540 --> 00:07:00.160
Tell me, when will the lord be going
to put down the monster of Tron Cavern?

00:07:00.160 --> 00:07:02.580
Yes indeed, I wonder when.

00:07:02.580 --> 00:07:03.870
Tron Cavern?

00:07:03.870 --> 00:07:04.910
You don't know about it?

00:07:04.910 --> 00:07:07.240
It comes from Magonian lore.

00:07:07.240 --> 00:07:08.790
There's a legend that says

00:07:08.790 --> 00:07:12.740
there's a shape-changing monster who lives
at the spring inside Tron Cavern.

00:07:12.740 --> 00:07:16.200
And that the monster
can transform into anything!

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:20.450
Like a dragon, or a snake, or even a giant wolf!

00:07:25.790 --> 00:07:27.040
Is something the matter?

00:07:27.040 --> 00:07:29.240
Oh, it's nothing.

00:07:29.240 --> 00:07:32.990
Aw, I wish I could go see it sometime.

00:07:32.990 --> 00:07:35.620
But as I understand it, that legend...

00:07:35.620 --> 00:07:39.490
Hmph, it's silly.
There's no way such a monster exists.

00:07:39.490 --> 00:07:40.490
Big Sister!

00:07:40.490 --> 00:07:44.870
The priest says that stories
about Magonia are all made up.

00:07:44.870 --> 00:07:46.660
It's not made up!

00:07:46.660 --> 00:07:50.240
Then go there and see for yourself.

00:07:50.240 --> 00:07:52.450
Hey, now.

00:07:52.450 --> 00:07:55.410
Alfred! Maurice!

00:07:55.410 --> 00:07:56.990
My lord!

00:07:56.990 --> 00:08:00.740
Listen, you two, Tron Cavern is too dangerous.
It's like a labyrinth.

00:08:00.740 --> 00:08:03.120
I told you, children shouldn't
go in there unaccompanied.

00:08:03.120 --> 00:08:07.490
Aww... I want to see the monster change shape!

00:08:07.490 --> 00:08:10.040
Into a dragon, or a snake, or a giant--

00:08:10.040 --> 00:08:11.040
Um--!

00:08:12.290 --> 00:08:14.910
Marius, is something the matter?

00:08:14.910 --> 00:08:19.990
I, uh... H-How dare you trick me, Alfred!

00:08:19.990 --> 00:08:20.620
Huh?

00:08:20.620 --> 00:08:24.990
An escort mission for Nonnoria?
I just ended up carrying her things!

00:08:24.990 --> 00:08:27.330
Oh, yeah, about that...

00:08:27.330 --> 00:08:31.200
It always looks so hard for her
to carry all that heavy stuff, so...

00:08:31.200 --> 00:08:33.910
I'm going to make <i>you</i> carry all of it later.

00:08:33.910 --> 00:08:35.700
Huh? No, you can't do that!

00:08:35.700 --> 00:08:38.080
--Yes I can. He has it coming!
--Ah, Conny!

00:08:39.450 --> 00:08:41.580
Fine then! I'll just go by myself!

00:08:41.580 --> 00:08:44.830
What are you talking about?
You don't have the guts.

00:08:44.830 --> 00:08:46.330
Yes I do!

00:08:48.330 --> 00:08:50.700
Considering the safety of the children,

00:08:50.700 --> 00:08:54.490
I think maybe we should go and check it out.

00:08:54.490 --> 00:08:56.540
Are you listening?

00:08:56.540 --> 00:08:58.830
Wah! Hot! Hot! Hot!

00:08:57.050 --> 00:08:58.830
Sorry, Qoo!

00:08:58.830 --> 00:09:00.080
Oh, dear!

00:09:01.830 --> 00:09:04.240
That was mean <i>moru</i> !

00:09:04.240 --> 00:09:05.700
Are you okay, Qoo?

00:09:05.700 --> 00:09:06.540
<i>Moru</i> ...

00:09:06.540 --> 00:09:08.290
Let's get you washed up!

00:09:08.290 --> 00:09:09.790
Let's do <i>moru</i> .

00:09:09.790 --> 00:09:10.790
You were saying...?

00:09:10.790 --> 00:09:12.790
The monster of Tron Cavern.

00:09:12.790 --> 00:09:13.580
Right...

00:09:13.580 --> 00:09:16.790
Hey now, that's just a legend, right?

00:09:16.790 --> 00:09:19.450
Indeed it is, but ever since Rugis's uprising,

00:09:19.450 --> 00:09:23.830
lots of monsters that had been imaginary
have been appearing across Hortensia.

00:09:23.830 --> 00:09:27.910
So it shouldn't be any wonder that
the monster of Tron Cavern is real.

00:09:27.910 --> 00:09:29.790
You're right.

00:09:29.790 --> 00:09:31.040
Marius, what do you think?

00:09:31.040 --> 00:09:37.740
Huh? Um, I think it would be best...
if we went and saw...

00:09:37.740 --> 00:09:40.200
All right, no time like the present.

00:09:40.200 --> 00:09:42.240
Let's be off at once.

00:09:51.450 --> 00:09:52.490
Sorry!

00:09:52.490 --> 00:09:53.910
It's nothing.

00:09:53.910 --> 00:09:55.950
Tron Cavern is just up ahead.

00:09:55.950 --> 00:09:57.370
Okay...

00:09:57.370 --> 00:09:58.620
Marius,

00:09:58.620 --> 00:10:00.200
is something the matter?

00:10:00.200 --> 00:10:01.580
Not especially.

00:10:03.160 --> 00:10:05.580
I can't stand wolves.

00:10:05.580 --> 00:10:08.490
We all have things that get to us.

00:10:08.490 --> 00:10:11.620
If a wolf shows up,
Maurice and I will take care of it.

00:10:15.790 --> 00:10:16.870
Alfred...

00:10:20.040 --> 00:10:24.330
I heard that your father
was killed by a werewolf.

00:10:27.580 --> 00:10:29.660
That's true.

00:10:29.660 --> 00:10:33.160
Haven't you ever found yourself hating werewolves?

00:10:33.160 --> 00:10:38.290
Dad stuck to his code of chivalry
and fought to the end.

00:10:38.290 --> 00:10:42.910
Regardless of what he was facing,
I don't mean to bear them any ill will.

00:10:42.910 --> 00:10:45.370
Do you really feel that way?

00:10:45.370 --> 00:10:46.370
Huh?

00:10:47.450 --> 00:10:51.620
What if it wasn't a werewolf that
brought about your father's death,

00:10:51.620 --> 00:10:53.660
but something else, instead?

00:10:53.660 --> 00:10:54.700
Huh?

00:10:54.700 --> 00:10:56.410
Hey!

00:10:56.410 --> 00:10:59.450
What are you two up to? We're burning daylight!

00:10:59.450 --> 00:11:00.870
Oh, sorry!

00:11:09.410 --> 00:11:10.790
My lord!

00:11:10.790 --> 00:11:12.790
My lord, are you in?!

00:11:12.790 --> 00:11:14.490
Coming!

00:11:14.490 --> 00:11:15.910
Who is it?

00:11:15.910 --> 00:11:16.870
Nonnoria!

00:11:16.870 --> 00:11:18.870
Auntie! And Doris, too!

00:11:18.870 --> 00:11:20.200
Is the lord in?

00:11:20.200 --> 00:11:24.580
Alfred went out to take care of monsters.

00:11:24.580 --> 00:11:25.870
Is something the matter?

00:11:25.870 --> 00:11:28.830
My Conny has gone missing!

00:11:28.830 --> 00:11:29.790
Huh?!

00:11:29.790 --> 00:11:32.790
He may have gone to Tron Cavern.

00:11:32.790 --> 00:11:34.160
Are you sure?

00:11:35.580 --> 00:11:39.660
He wants to get me to believe that
the monster at the spring is real.

00:11:39.660 --> 00:11:41.160
This is my fault!

00:11:41.160 --> 00:11:45.540
It's all right. Alfred and the others
are at Tron Cavern right now.

00:11:45.540 --> 00:11:47.830
But he said it was like a labyrinth in there <i>moru</i> .

00:11:47.830 --> 00:11:49.700
They may miss each other <i>moru</i> !

00:11:51.580 --> 00:11:57.580
Doris, don't worry. You just leave everything to me!

00:11:57.580 --> 00:12:01.290
This is terrible! This is terrible!

00:12:01.290 --> 00:12:04.120
Nonnoria, it's too dangerous for you to go alone <i>moru</i> .

00:12:04.120 --> 00:12:06.080
I know!

00:12:06.080 --> 00:12:10.580
But right now, time is of the essence!

00:12:10.580 --> 00:12:12.200
Wait for me <i>moru</i> !

00:12:12.200 --> 00:12:14.540
Conny, sit tight!

00:12:14.540 --> 00:12:18.040
Nonnoria is coming to the rescue right now!

00:12:25.290 --> 00:12:26.370
Behind you!

00:12:29.120 --> 00:12:31.790
I wasn't expecting this to have become a monster den.

00:12:31.790 --> 00:12:35.370
Yeah. It's a good thing we came to investigate.

00:12:35.370 --> 00:12:36.870
Dead end.

00:12:36.870 --> 00:12:39.200
Let's call it a day.

00:12:40.870 --> 00:12:43.080
Now we go back the way we came.

00:12:43.080 --> 00:12:45.540
Let's take care not to get lost.

00:12:46.950 --> 00:12:49.040
We're lost.

00:12:49.040 --> 00:12:52.910
I get the feeling that we've been
going in circles for a while <i>moru</i> .

00:12:54.910 --> 00:12:57.870
Where are you, Conny?

00:13:05.450 --> 00:13:07.790
Wh-Wh-Why are there someone's bones down here?!

00:13:07.790 --> 00:13:09.200
Those aren't Conny's, are they?

00:13:09.200 --> 00:13:10.950
They can't be!

00:13:14.740 --> 00:13:16.740
Someone is crying <i>moru</i> .

00:13:18.160 --> 00:13:19.950
You don't suppose that's...?

00:13:23.830 --> 00:13:24.910
Conny!

00:13:24.910 --> 00:13:26.660
Nonnoria!

00:13:26.660 --> 00:13:28.330
You're all right <i>moru</i> !

00:13:28.330 --> 00:13:30.660
Thank goodness!

00:13:30.660 --> 00:13:34.290
I got lost down here, and my lamp went out...

00:13:34.290 --> 00:13:37.580
I didn't think I'd ever get out of here again...

00:13:37.580 --> 00:13:41.290
Now that I'm here, you can take it easy.

00:13:41.290 --> 00:13:43.290
Okay, let's get you home!

00:13:43.290 --> 00:13:43.800
Mm-hmm!

00:13:43.800 --> 00:13:45.120
<i>Moru</i> !

00:13:46.790 --> 00:13:48.790
What's the matter?

00:13:48.790 --> 00:13:50.830
We're lost, too.

00:13:50.830 --> 00:13:51.390
<i>Moru</i> ...

00:13:51.390 --> 00:13:52.910
Huh?

00:13:52.910 --> 00:13:56.370
No problem, no problem!
If we keep moving, we'll find our way!

00:13:58.540 --> 00:14:00.200
Run <i>moru</i> !

00:14:02.450 --> 00:14:03.110
Your ribbon!

00:14:03.110 --> 00:14:04.950
It's okay! Hurry!

00:14:07.660 --> 00:14:09.950
Wh-Wh-What do we do <i>moru</i> ?

00:14:09.950 --> 00:14:12.160
We'll be trapped like rats <i>moru</i> !

00:14:12.160 --> 00:14:15.950
This calls for my secret weapon!

00:14:20.700 --> 00:14:25.240
Distract the monsters with meat,
and while they're busy, run for it.

00:14:26.290 --> 00:14:27.410
Now!

00:14:30.490 --> 00:14:31.370
Nonnoria!

00:14:31.370 --> 00:14:32.490
Whoops!

00:14:32.490 --> 00:14:34.450
Hurry <i>moru</i> !

00:14:34.450 --> 00:14:35.140
They're in front of us, too!

00:14:35.140 --> 00:14:36.740
We're surrounded <i>moru</i> !

00:14:36.740 --> 00:14:37.950
<i>Moru</i> !

00:14:38.950 --> 00:14:40.410
Oh, no!

00:14:40.410 --> 00:14:42.700
We're done for <i>moru</i> .

00:14:42.700 --> 00:14:43.870
Mommy!

00:14:43.870 --> 00:14:46.830
I-It's all right. It's at a moment like this...

00:14:46.830 --> 00:14:49.660
...when he's sure to come to our rescue.

00:14:49.660 --> 00:14:52.120
I have faith!

00:14:52.120 --> 00:14:54.080
Just like he did before!

00:14:54.080 --> 00:14:55.450
I'm sure...

00:14:57.240 --> 00:14:58.660
Alfred!

00:15:03.450 --> 00:15:05.160
Alfred!

00:15:06.740 --> 00:15:09.160
Marius! Maurice!

00:15:09.160 --> 00:15:11.040
Is anyone hurt?

00:15:12.410 --> 00:15:13.870
Sorry we took so long.

00:15:20.540 --> 00:15:27.370
I believed in you! I believed that
you would come and rescue us!

00:15:27.370 --> 00:15:28.620
It's all thanks to this.

00:15:28.620 --> 00:15:31.450
Huh? My ribbon?

00:15:31.450 --> 00:15:34.910
Marius noticed that it had fallen on the ground.

00:15:34.910 --> 00:15:37.660
Marius, I owe you my life!

00:15:37.660 --> 00:15:39.700
I'm bursting with gratitude!

00:15:41.660 --> 00:15:43.990
There.

00:15:43.990 --> 00:15:47.580
Don't do anything too crazy, okay, Nonnoria?

00:15:47.580 --> 00:15:49.410
Alfred...

00:15:50.580 --> 00:15:54.410
Now, let's get out of here before
any other monsters show up.

00:15:54.410 --> 00:15:55.790
R-Right!

00:15:55.790 --> 00:15:57.870
Sorry to be such a burden!

00:16:00.290 --> 00:16:02.120
What's that?

00:16:02.120 --> 00:16:04.950
Something's glowing <i>moru</i> .

00:16:04.950 --> 00:16:06.740
Everyone wait here.

00:16:06.740 --> 00:16:08.870
Hey, I'm coming too!

00:16:19.740 --> 00:16:21.910
This must be the spring of Tron Cavern.

00:16:25.580 --> 00:16:27.410
Alfred...

00:16:27.410 --> 00:16:30.080
It's okay. This is moonlight.

00:16:40.870 --> 00:16:42.580
What's that?!

00:16:42.580 --> 00:16:45.240
Is that... a werewolf?

00:16:45.240 --> 00:16:47.040
It can't be...

00:16:47.040 --> 00:16:48.700
What is he doing here?!

00:16:57.990 --> 00:17:00.790
Look alive, Alfred!

00:17:00.790 --> 00:17:02.490
Are you...

00:17:02.490 --> 00:17:05.410
Are you the werewolf who killed Dad?!

00:17:05.410 --> 00:17:10.990
This is an imposter!
Not the werewolf that killed your old man!

00:17:10.990 --> 00:17:12.200
Marius!

00:17:18.330 --> 00:17:20.790
Why...?

00:17:20.790 --> 00:17:23.740
Why did this happen...?

00:17:23.740 --> 00:17:28.290
Father... Leon... Fernando...

00:17:28.290 --> 00:17:33.410
Princess, I know this is hard, but please
bear with it for a little while longer.

00:17:33.410 --> 00:17:35.080
You, too, Maurice...

00:17:35.080 --> 00:17:37.240
This isn't anything serious.

00:17:37.240 --> 00:17:39.620
What in the world was that?

00:17:39.620 --> 00:17:41.910
I don't know why it appeared here,

00:17:41.910 --> 00:17:44.990
nor do I know why it attacked the king,

00:17:44.990 --> 00:17:47.290
but it was a werewolf,

00:17:47.290 --> 00:17:49.700
right out of Magonian lore.

00:17:49.700 --> 00:17:51.160
A werewolf?

00:17:53.200 --> 00:17:54.240
Maurice!

00:17:57.040 --> 00:17:59.830
Old Man Balthauser!

00:17:59.830 --> 00:18:01.490
This way. Hurry.

00:18:07.620 --> 00:18:10.290
Go through here.
You should be able to get outside the castle

00:18:10.290 --> 00:18:14.080
without encountering any Camellian forces or monsters.

00:18:14.080 --> 00:18:16.160
Thanks, old man.

00:18:16.160 --> 00:18:19.740
Okay, Princess Mariel.
You, too, old man, quickly.

00:18:19.740 --> 00:18:21.240
Listen to me, Maurice.

00:18:22.870 --> 00:18:25.080
There have long been those hidden in the capital

00:18:25.080 --> 00:18:29.830
who have been trying to make
the royal family their puppets.

00:18:29.830 --> 00:18:32.200
And in the middle of this chaos,

00:18:32.200 --> 00:18:36.120
Prince Charlot has been secured
by Pope Vall d'Hebron.

00:18:36.120 --> 00:18:37.990
You aren't saying the pope is...?

00:18:37.990 --> 00:18:39.910
I can't say for sure.

00:18:39.910 --> 00:18:42.990
But ever since he took the papal throne,

00:18:42.990 --> 00:18:47.080
His Majesty started changing, bit by bit.

00:18:47.080 --> 00:18:49.990
It's possible that this uprising might be...

00:18:49.990 --> 00:18:52.080
So, is Charlot all right?

00:18:54.490 --> 00:18:59.990
Maurice, I will remain here to keep Prince Charlot safe.

00:18:59.990 --> 00:19:01.580
You take care of the princess.

00:19:01.580 --> 00:19:03.370
I want to help Charlot, too!

00:19:03.370 --> 00:19:04.700
You mustn't!

00:19:04.700 --> 00:19:08.700
Princess Mariel, go with Maurice,
someplace beyond the reach of the pope.

00:19:08.700 --> 00:19:10.620
No! Let me go!

00:19:10.620 --> 00:19:13.410
Keep yourself in hiding until the time comes.

00:19:13.410 --> 00:19:16.290
Charlot! Charlot!

00:19:19.410 --> 00:19:22.410
We're going to head for the Albert Dominion.

00:19:22.410 --> 00:19:24.790
It's the territory my brother governed.

00:19:24.790 --> 00:19:28.580
I believe it to be the safest place for you, Princess.

00:19:28.580 --> 00:19:29.910
Fernando's land?

00:19:32.580 --> 00:19:34.290
It can't be, Dad!

00:19:36.740 --> 00:19:38.040
It can't be!

00:19:40.490 --> 00:19:42.870
Alfred...

00:19:42.870 --> 00:19:44.330
I...

00:19:46.040 --> 00:19:47.040
Marius...

00:19:48.870 --> 00:19:49.870
Marius!

00:19:50.620 --> 00:19:52.580
Shake it off, Marius!

00:20:01.740 --> 00:20:03.370
Are you all right?

00:20:03.370 --> 00:20:05.200
Yeah, thanks.

00:20:05.200 --> 00:20:06.580
Good.

00:20:06.580 --> 00:20:09.450
Where's the werewolf?

00:20:09.450 --> 00:20:11.160
That is no werewolf.

00:20:13.740 --> 00:20:16.990
That is the monster of Tron Cavern.

00:20:16.990 --> 00:20:20.870
Ber told me about it a long time ago.

00:20:20.870 --> 00:20:24.740
There's a mysterious spring deep inside Tron Cavern.

00:20:24.740 --> 00:20:29.490
The monster that lives there reads the minds
of those who come to the spring,

00:20:29.490 --> 00:20:33.370
and takes the form of whatever
that person hates the most.

00:20:34.620 --> 00:20:37.660
Then that must have been from my mind.

00:20:47.700 --> 00:20:49.040
Mother!

00:20:49.040 --> 00:20:50.910
Big Sister!

00:20:50.910 --> 00:20:52.950
Conny!

00:20:52.950 --> 00:20:54.790
Thank goodness you're all right, Conny!

00:20:54.790 --> 00:20:56.330
I'm sorry, Mother!

00:20:56.330 --> 00:20:57.480
That's all right!

00:20:56.650 --> 00:20:59.580
I'm sorry, Conny. This is my fault.

00:20:59.580 --> 00:21:02.080
Mm-mm, that's not true.

00:21:02.080 --> 00:21:04.040
And all's well that ends well.

00:21:02.080 --> 00:21:04.040
I'm sorry I worried you.

00:21:04.040 --> 00:21:06.660
That's all right.

00:21:05.110 --> 00:21:06.660
Nonnoria...

00:21:06.660 --> 00:21:07.320
Yes?

00:21:07.320 --> 00:21:08.120
You too, Qoo.

00:21:08.120 --> 00:21:09.490
<i>Moru</i> ?

00:21:09.490 --> 00:21:14.040
I can't believe you went someplace so dangerous,
even to rescue someone.

00:21:14.040 --> 00:21:17.370
What am I supposed to do if I lose you, too?

00:21:18.330 --> 00:21:19.330
<i>Moru</i> ...

00:21:21.290 --> 00:21:23.450
You're all like dear family to me.

00:21:26.490 --> 00:21:28.450
--Alfred!
-- <i>Moru</i> !

00:21:28.450 --> 00:21:30.870
--We're sorry!
--We're sorry <i>moru</i> !

00:21:32.240 --> 00:21:33.450
We're sorry!

00:21:33.450 --> 00:21:35.450
Henceforth,

00:21:35.450 --> 00:21:39.120
you will have to live under
an assumed identity, after all.

00:21:42.870 --> 00:21:43.910
Marius...

00:21:46.080 --> 00:21:47.120
Alfred...

00:21:48.790 --> 00:21:50.040
Let's go home.

00:21:51.490 --> 00:21:52.490
Yeah.

00:21:58.420 --> 00:22:02.080
Chapter 2

00:21:58.420 --> 00:22:02.080
Memories

00:21:58.420 --> 00:22:02.080
~The Lore of Magonia~

00:23:32.830 --> 00:23:35.040
Those accusations are false!

00:23:35.040 --> 00:23:36.620
You invited us personally, after all.

00:23:36.620 --> 00:23:39.410
Sounds just like the undead of Magonian lore.

00:23:39.410 --> 00:23:41.240
Don't be ridiculous! Of course not!

00:23:41.240 --> 00:23:44.080
The Orthodox Church sacrificed this village.

00:23:44.080 --> 00:23:47.070
Chapter 3

00:23:44.080 --> 00:23:47.070
Repose                  of Souls

00:23:44.080 --> 00:23:47.070
~To the Quarantined Village~

00:23:44.080 --> 00:23:46.540
None of your business.
